---
title: Lookalike Connected App Authorized via Vishing-Style Support Flow
id: 7c9d1e2f-3a4b-4c6d-e5f6-8a9b0c1d2e01
status: experimental
description: Detects authorization of a new SaaS connected app whose name resembles a known IT/support tool, matching ShinyHunters' vishing-driven initial access pattern where a caller walks an employee through approving a lookalike app.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0059/
    - https://www.huntress.com/threat-library/threat-actors/shinyhunters
tags:
    - attack.initial_access
    - attack.t1566.004
    - attack.t1528
logsource:
    category: application
    service: saas_audit
detection:
    selection:
        Action: 'ConnectedApp Authorization'
        AppName|contains:
            - 'Support'
            - 'IT Helper'
            - 'Verify'
            - 'Sync Tool'
    filter_known_good:
        AppName|contains: 'APPROVED_APP_ALLOWLIST'  # populate with vetted app names
    condition: selection and not filter_known_good
falsepositives:
    - Legitimately named internal or vendor-approved integration matching a generic keyword
level: medium

---
title: Credential Reuse Login from Infostealer-Associated IP or ASN
id: 7c9d1e2f-3a4b-4c6d-e5f6-8a9b0c1d2e02
status: experimental
description: Detects a successful login using credentials recently observed in infostealer log dumps or from infrastructure associated with credential marketplaces, matching ShinyHunters' reuse of stolen or purchased credentials.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.huntress.com/threat-library/threat-actors/shinyhunters
tags:
    - attack.initial_access
    - attack.t1078
logsource:
    category: authentication
detection:
    selection:
        EventType: 'LoginSuccess'
        SourceIp|cidr: KNOWN_INFOSTEALER_IOC_LIST  # populate via current threat intel feed
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Shared/dynamic IP address reused by an unrelated legitimate user after the flagged session
level: medium

---
title: OAuth Refresh Token Used from New Third-Party Integration Without Login Event
id: 7c9d1e2f-3a4b-4c6d-e5f6-8a9b0c1d2e03
status: experimental
description: Detects API activity authenticated via a stored OAuth refresh token from a third-party SaaS integration (e.g. Drift, Gainsight) accessing Salesforce data without a corresponding interactive login, matching ShinyHunters' token abuse to reach connected environments quietly.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1528/
tags:
    - attack.persistence
    - attack.t1528
logsource:
    category: application
    product: salesforce
    service: login_history
detection:
    selection:
        LoginType: 'OAuth-Refresh-Token'
        AppName|contains:
            - 'Drift'
            - 'Gainsight'
    filter_known_good:
        AppName|contains: 'APPROVED_INTEGRATION_LIST'  # populate with sanctioned third-party integrations
    condition: selection and not filter_known_good
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate ongoing use of a sanctioned third-party CRM integration
level: medium

---
title: Session Cookie Reuse After Credential Rotation
id: 7c9d1e2f-3a4b-4c6d-e5f6-8a9b0c1d2e04
status: experimental
description: Detects continued authenticated activity under a session token that predates a recent password reset for the same account, consistent with ShinyHunters' use of stolen session cookies to persist through credential rotation.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1556/003/
tags:
    - attack.defense_evasion
    - attack.t1556.003
logsource:
    category: application
    service: identity_provider
detection:
    selection_reset:
        OperationName: 'Reset password (self-service or admin)'
    selection_old_session:
        SessionCreatedTime|lt: 'field:PasswordResetTime'
        EventType: 'AuthenticatedRequest'
    timeframe: 24h
    condition: selection_reset and selection_old_session
falsepositives:
    - Session revocation delay in identity provider allowing a brief valid overlap window
level: high

---
title: Gmail Add-On Authorized with Mail Deletion Scope
id: 7c9d1e2f-3a4b-4c6d-e5f6-8a9b0c1d2e05
status: experimental
description: Detects authorization of a Google Workspace add-on requesting mail deletion or modify scopes, matching ShinyHunters' reported technique of silently deleting MFA enrollment notification emails to delay detection.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.huntress.com/threat-library/threat-actors/shinyhunters
tags:
    - attack.defense_evasion
    - attack.t1564
logsource:
    category: application
    service: gsuite_activity
detection:
    selection:
        EventType: 'AUTHORIZE'
        ScopeData|contains:
            - 'gmail.modify'
            - 'gmail.settings.basic'
    filter_known_good:
        AppName|contains: 'APPROVED_GSUITE_ADDON_LIST'  # populate with vetted add-ons
    condition: selection and not filter_known_good
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate email-management add-on (unsubscribe tools, cleanup utilities) approved by the user
level: high

---
title: Bulk Export or API Pull from Snowflake/BigQuery Outside Business Hours
id: 7c9d1e2f-3a4b-4c6d-e5f6-8a9b0c1d2e06
status: experimental
description: Detects a large-volume query or export job against a Snowflake warehouse or BigQuery dataset executed outside normal business hours, matching ShinyHunters' collection stage which precedes extortion in several disclosed cases.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1530/
tags:
    - attack.collection
    - attack.t1530
    - attack.exfiltration
logsource:
    category: application
    service: data_warehouse_audit
detection:
    selection:
        QueryType:
            - 'COPY INTO'
            - 'EXPORT DATA'
            - 'SELECT'
        RowsReturned|gt: 100000
    timeframe_filter:
        QueryHourUTC|gte: 22
    condition: selection and timeframe_filter
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate scheduled ETL or reporting job running during off-hours
level: medium

---
title: Bulk Native Export Activity from Compromised SaaS Admin Session
id: 7c9d1e2f-3a4b-4c6d-e5f6-8a9b0c1d2e07
status: experimental
description: Detects repeated use of a platform's own export/report functionality generating an unusually high volume of records within a short window, matching ShinyHunters' preference for exfiltrating via legitimate native tooling to blend with admin activity.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.huntress.com/threat-library/threat-actors/shinyhunters
tags:
    - attack.exfiltration
    - attack.t1567.002
    - attack.collection
logsource:
    category: application
    service: saas_audit
detection:
    selection:
        Action:
            - 'ReportExport'
            - 'BulkDataExport'
    condition: selection | count(RequestId) by UserId > 20
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate bulk reporting or scheduled data sync by an authorized admin
level: medium

